   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Crumple Toss\n\nA card crumples into a paper wad in stop-motion poses and is tossed into a bin: the old way, thrown away.\n\nCategory: paper. Length: 3 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- An outdated process, old way or rejected idea should visibly be crumpled up and thrown away before the new one appears.\n- A paper, stop-motion look is wanted.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The card must stay legible while it leaves: this destroys it.\n- You want a smooth, digital exit rather than discrete stop-motion poses.\n\nVariables:\n- card_title (string): Card title, default \"How it used to work\"\n- card_body (string): Card text, default \"Six steps and a wiki page\"\n- at (number, 0-60): Start frame, default 6\n- crumple_steps (number, 1-10): Crumple poses, default 4\n- toss_steps (number, 1-12): Toss poses, default 5\n- direction (number, -180-180): Direction, default -35\n- distance (number, 100-900): Distance, default 440\n- spin (number, -720-720): Spin, default 220\n- segments (number, 3-16): Segments, default 9\n- layers (number, 1-4): Layers, default 2\n- randomness (number, 0-1): Randomness, default 0.6\n- crush_to (number, 0.15-0.8): Crush to, default 0.34\n- seed (string): Seed, default \"toss\"\n- step (number, 1-6): Frames per pose, default 3\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
